# Core conventions

Read [`AGENTS.md`](mdc:AGENTS.md) and [`PROJECT_MAP.md`](mdc:PROJECT_MAP.md)
before making non-trivial edits. They are the canonical source of truth
about layout and intent.

## Hard rules — do NOT violate

- **No autonomous trading bots.** Paper-trading bots (stock + index)
  were removed from this app. Do not reintroduce decision engines, order
  simulators, position managers, ledgers, or any "auto" trade-management
  scheduler that opens, closes, or sizes positions. The app is now
  read-only analysis: screener + index analysis + live verification +
  live observation.
- **No real broker SDK or live order placement.** Ever.
- Every screener / index signal carries a stop-loss / invalidation level.
  Never return a trade plan without one.
- User-facing AI output ends with: *"Research and decision-support only.
  Not financial advice."* — keep this verbatim.
- Backtests / look-back analysis must not have look-ahead. Slice CSV with
  `df[: as_of]` then recompute indicators on that slice.

## Comment style

```python
# BAD — narrates what the code does
# Loop over signals and apply the rule engine
for signal in signals:
    engine.evaluate(signal)

# GOOD — explains WHY (a non-obvious constraint)
# Skip pre-aggregation: ranking depends on per-signal score which is only
# finalised after risk adjustments downstream.
for signal in signals:
    engine.evaluate(signal)
```

## After substantive edits

- Backend: `cd backend && .\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -m pytest -q`
- Frontend: `cd frontend && npx tsc --noEmit && npm run build`
- Use the `ReadLints` tool on touched files.

## Don't add

- New top-level files unless absolutely necessary.
- New dependencies without clear justification.
- Comments that just translate code into English.
- Auto-trading code paths (decision/sizing/simulator/scheduler-driven
  position management). The app is intentionally read-only.
